<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Olof Skötkonung</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 980–1022</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Olof Skötkonung was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> from about 995 and the first Swedish king known to have been a Christian, traditionally baptised at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husaby">Husaby</a>. Son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-the-victorious">Eric the Victorious</a>, he ruled both the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/svear">Svear</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geats">Geats</a>, a union regarded as the beginning of the medieval Kingdom of Sweden, and minted the first Swedish coins at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigtuna">Sigtuna</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/olof-skotkonung.jpg" alt="Olof Skötkonung" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown 11th century mintmaster; photo/scan by unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Olaf_Scotking_of_Sweden_coin_c_1030.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
